
1.server manager
2.click on tools
3.click on services
4.slect "open ssh authentication"
5.right click on it and go to properties
6.select 'status type' to 'automatic' and click on start
7.apply and finish
8. Press the Win + R keys, type wf.msc, and press Enter to open Windows Defender Firewall with Advanced Security.
9.In the left-hand pane, click on Inbound Rules.
10.In the right-hand Actions pane, click New Rule....
11. Choose Port and click Next.
12. Select TCP and type 22 in the Specific local ports field, then click Next.
13.Choose Allow the connection and click Next.
14. Select the network profiles (Domain, Private, Public) where you want this rule applied (usually Domain and Private are safest) and click Next.
15.Name the rule (e.g., SSH Port 22) and click Finish.
